<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Latvian Socialist Soviet Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Latvian Socialist Soviet Republic was a Bolshevik state proclaimed in December 1918 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peteris-stucka">Pēteris Stučka</a> and backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a>, which took Riga in January 1919. Its rule brought revolutionary tribunals, requisitions and famine in the capital. It collapsed after losing Riga in May 1919 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latgale">Latgale</a> in early 1920, and Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> recognised Latvian independence in August 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/latvian-socialist-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Latvian Socialist Soviet Republic" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Latvian_Socialist_Soviet_Republic_(1918%E2%80%931920).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
